          }' data-animation=none data-controllers-bound=SectionWrapperController data-active=true>
 <div class=section-border>
 <div class=section-background>
 
 
 
 </div>
 </div>
 <div class=content-wrapper>
 <div class=content>
 
 
 
 
 
 
 <div class="sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12" data-type=page-section id=page-section-61fec7b6c443042350d2c2a2><div class="row sqs-row"><div class="col sqs-col-12 span-12"><div class="row sqs-row"><div class="col sqs-col-6 span-6"><div class="sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html" data-block-type=2 id=block-55f3c7b340300af9c4f4><div class=sqs-block-content>
<h2 style=white-space:pre-wrap>Problem</h2><p class=sqsrte-large style=white-space:pre-wrap>NdFeB Magnets are the strongest permanent magnets on earth<strong> </strong>and <strong>critical to most clean energy technologies</strong>.<p style=white-space:pre-wrap>Since the invention of this magnet, new fields of application have appeared every year, with an annual growth in demand of <span class=sqsrte-text-color--accent><strong>more than 30%</strong></span><strong>.</strong><p style=white-space:pre-wrap>Although there are thousands of recyclers in the U.S., <span class=sqsrte-text-color--accent><strong>none </strong></span>have a profitable method for recovering highly valuable REEs from NdFeB magnets.  Thus, they are shredded and sold as contaminated scrap metal.</p>
</div></div></div><div class="col sqs-col-1 span-1"><div class="sqs-block spacer-block sqs-block-spacer sized vsize-1" data-block-type=21 id=block-3f21ac4f9df18ca4c46c><div class=sqs-block-content>&nbsp;</div></div></div><div class="col sqs-col-5 span-5"><div class="sqs-block spacer-block sqs-block-spacer sized vsize-1" data-block-type=21 id=block-yui_3_17_2_1_1645499929228_18131><div class=sqs-block-content>&nbsp;</div></div><div class="sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html" data-block-type=2 id=block-459b7719a4bc0d24ca7c><div class=sqs-block-content>
<p style=white-space:pre-wrap><span class=sqsrte-text-color--custom style=color:#BD0D0D>✘</span> <strong>Demand is expected to surpass</strong> supply.<p style=white-space:pre-wrap><span class=sqsrte-text-color--custom style=color:#BD0D0D>✘</span> <strong>There are no substitutes</strong> for REEs that can create the same performance.<p style=white-space:pre-wrap><span class=sqsrte-text-color--custom style=color:#BD0D0D>✘</span> <strong>China controls 97%</strong> of the REEs used in magnets.<p style=white-space:pre-wrap><span class=sqsrte-text-color--custom style=color:#BD0D0D>✘</span> <strong>Trade war exposure</strong> to supply chains for OEMs worldwide.<p style=white-space:pre-wrap><span class=sqsrte-text-color--custom style=color:#BD0D0D>✘</span> <strong>Increasing concern of environmental impacts</strong> from mining and processing.</p>
</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 
</section>
 
 
 
 
